  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Michigan's 10th Congressional District is an open seat after Republican incumbent John James decided to run for governor rather than seek re-election. The district covers southern Macomb County and portions of eastern Oakland County including Rochester and Rochester Hills, and has a Cook Partisan Voting Index of R+3. Cook Political Report rates the general election as Lean Republican. Three Democrats and four Republicans are competing in the August 4, 2026 primary for the right to succeed James in this competitive suburban Detroit district, which Republicans have held since 2022 after John James flipped it from Democratic control.",
